            <ArticleTitle>Subdural haematoma associated with an arachnoid cyst after repetitive minor heading injury in ball games.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a chronic subdural haematoma caused by repetitive heading of a football which led to the diagnosis of a middle fossa arachnoid cyst. The association between arachnoid cysts and subdural haematoma is discussed as are safety implications in sporting injuries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
